📚 Resource in MCP (Model Context Protocol)
🎯 What is a Resource?

A Resource in MCP is readable data that an AI model can access from an MCP server.

Think of a resource as a file, document, database record, log, or any information source that the AI can read when it needs context.

Simple Definition:

A Resource is information exposed by an MCP server for AI to read.

Unlike tools, resources do not perform actions. They simply provide data.


🤔 Why Do We Need Resources?

AI models have limited built-in knowledge about your private or current data.

Resources allow an AI to read information like:

Documentation
PDFs
Configuration files
Source code
Logs
Database records
API specifications
Project notes

Instead of guessing, the AI reads the actual data.

🧠 Core Idea

A Resource is:

Read-only
Structured or unstructured data
Shared by the MCP Server
Used to give the AI additional context

The AI reads it but doesn't execute it.
